WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:08.690
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.990
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.700
but also in crime.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.950
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.540
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.540
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.190
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.990
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:58.990
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.370
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.210
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:18.430
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:25.020
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:31.360
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:37.150
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:43.700
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.380
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:01.140
Go to Demon Mountain!

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:10.400
Now, gentlemen,
let's sing "The Green Pastures."

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:22.910
Oh, the wide pasture
is so green

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:26.830
A sea of grass with
winds blowing across

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:30.080
Oh, the wide pasture
is so green

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.300
Look how overgrown
it's become!

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:35.130
Hey!

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.010
Hey?

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:40.050
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:43.180
It isn't "hey." The lyrics are...

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:47.020
"Look how overgrown
it's become, eh!"

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:48.140
Right?

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:52.560
I can accept that
you're shy, and sing off-key...

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:56.650
but don't ruin the mood
for us, okay? It's "eh!"

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:57.530
Hey.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.990
You blockhead!
It's "eh!" "Eh!"

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:05.540
We're trying to escape the urban
life, become one with nature!

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.500
Get with the program!

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:16.800
What is that?

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:23.390
Something's
passed this way!

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:27.720
Passed this way? What could
possibly do this?

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:30.270
It was huge,
whatever it was!

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:41.110
Something's there!

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:45.070
Don't say that! What if a bear
came out? What could we do?

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:50.000
You idiot! There aren't
any bears that strong!

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.040
You've seen too many
monster movies.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:55.000
What if it's...
more than a bear?

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:57.710
That's possible.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.670
You idiot!

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:10.980
Save me!
I'm too young to die!

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:13.560
I want to get married!

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.410
Hey, it's just a Labor!

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:30.290
The hand of man sets foot
in the forest this far.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:33.250
How dare it scare us like that!

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:48.050
It wasn't my fault!

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:54.100
Did you hear that?

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:58.560
That didn't sound
like a Labor.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.990
Hello, 911 Emergency. Yes?

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:12.790
A monster?

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:18.670
You saw a ten-meter-tall bear?
Oh, it might have been a cat.

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:21.710
A monkey?

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:26.930
Listen, the police don't have
time to chase hallucinations.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:31.310
Maybe you should call
the self-defense force.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:38.650
Hold on! We can't give this to
the army. It's our jurisdiction.

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:43.320
I'm afraid we'll
have to call... THEM.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:45.650
A mysterious giant creature?

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:50.410
We're not really
equipped to handle that.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.040
Yes, but...

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:56.580
What was that?

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:58.460
Monster control.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:03.710
Thank goodness my team
isn't on call this week.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:05.260
Have a heart.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:08.380
Monsters?
It's got to be a false alarm.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.970
But it's a good opportunity
for sightseeing.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:15.730
...so we're heading out.
Any questions?

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:20.230
Yes, Sir! Where are we going,
and what will we do there?

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:21.560
Do I have to tell you?

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:24.440
Aren't you going to
tell us anything?

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:27.700
There are some perplexing
elements to the original report.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.910
There may or may not be...

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:33.200
a giant creature in the forest.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:36.660
You mean...
a MONSTER!

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:38.620
It's obviously a Labor.

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:42.420
There have been cases
of Labors in costume.

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:43.790
Really?

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:46.090
Can this monster fly?

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:47.130
It's a LABOR.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.470
No one's perfected a Labor
that can move like an animal.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:53.970
But all the animals
that size are extinct.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:55.930
What about an elephant?

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:59.600
Let's go kill it!
We can identify it afterwards!

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:00.560
I suppose so.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:27.210
We're sure of it! Parts from
the Labor fell everywhere!

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:28.510
These are parts, all right.

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:32.300
So where's the main body?
Did your monster scare it away?

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:36.060
No, it was far too damaged
to move. But it was here!

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:41.890
And then there was a cry that
came from the depths of Hell!

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:46.150
It came from the heart of the
forest, with huge, evil eyes!

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.280
It's absolutely true!
Don't you believe us?

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:54.280
It's hard to believe in an
animal that's ten meters tall.

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.910
But it's true!

00:07:55.950 --> 00:08:00.540
Then there's the issue
of your vanishing Labor.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:06.340
My backpack!

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.210
Something was
chewing on it!

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:12.720
It was after our food.
Does a Labor need food?

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:15.510
This proves it!

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:21.390
Something's been
drooling on my backpack!

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:34.240
Maybe we should turn back,
and wait for the Labor team.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:36.320
Good idea! Let's go!

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:50.590
Get down! Crawl
so it doesn't see you.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:53.510
Hurry! Get in the car!

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:04.690
What was that?

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:07.440
Do you believe us now?

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:12.650
In 30 years, I've never
seen anything like that!

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:15.650
Then...

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:16.700
What?

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:19.410
It's a space alien!

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.000
Glad you're here.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:34.010
So, this baggage is
the pride of HQ.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:40.760
They've been called money pits,
jokes, and a useless waste.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:43.560
But still, they really
are the pride of HQ.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:45.310
What's the situation?

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:48.560
There really is
something out there.

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:51.400
So it's true.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:52.530
Yes.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:54.530
We'll get right on it.

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:59.530
Wait.
I don't suppose...

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:01.530
You want it captured alive?

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:07.960
A monster could
really boost tourism.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:11.790
That's what they're
thinking down in City Hall.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:18.630
Captain,
don't we have instructions yet?

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:21.140
Just a little longer, please.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:25.390
In a worst-case scenario,
couldn't we just have it stuffed?

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:29.900
Procedure
when confronting a target...

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:32.650
1: Call for a surrender.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:37.820
2: Thrust the baton into
a noncritical component.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:42.450
Officer Izumi, those are the
procedures for a manned Labor.

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:48.460
Yeah, but the manual doesn't
say anything about monsters.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:53.880
The Ingram's speed is its
main advantage in a fight.

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:58.220
You'd have a very tough
time against a live animal.

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:02.260
You sound so happy.

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:06.270
A Labor vs. a giant monster!
It stirs the blood, doesn't it?

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:08.230
How could you?

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:10.940
Time for a council of war!

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:13.150
He's weird.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.400
Any ideas on strategy?

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:18.070
We'll have to play it by ear.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:21.990
We don't know enough
to plan a strategy.

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:24.490
Sorry, that was poorly worded.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:27.330
When we find the beast...

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:33.920
should we emphasize
offense or defense?

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:36.380
Come on...
he's the pilot of machine 2.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:39.800
Captain, can we go now?

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:41.840
Why'd I bother to ask?

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:45.180
Here it comes!

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:48.310
It's coming!

00:11:57.730 --> 00:12:01.740
Dolphin

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:06.740
Crabman

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:11.660
Over here! The trail leads
back toward the mountains!

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:14.000
Team 2 is on
the south trail.

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:16.290
Team 3 has the
western trailhead.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:19.920
The carriers and team 1
are at the central trailhead.

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:25.640
With no warning, my birds
suddenly flew into a panic!

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:29.470
This huge black thing appeared!
It was after the birds!

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:32.810
They took off in the
direction of Seashore Hill.

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:35.650
A huge black thing?

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:42.610
I've lived here 60 years, and
I've never seen anything like it.

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:46.530
So anyway...

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:50.700
It must be a carnivore,
if it's after birds.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:53.290
It must have run out of
food in the mountains.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:57.250
But if it can't
find enough to eat...

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:00.210
It may start
attacking humans.

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:16.150
That idiot! Doesn't he
remember we're back here?

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:19.570
Is he really a policeman?
He keeps changing course.

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:22.230
And look at this
path of destruction!

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:32.040
Machine 2, try to move
a bit more efficiently.

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:35.500
The monsters aren't worried
about being efficient.

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:38.710
This ancient forest
isn't your enemy.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:42.630
What's the big deal if I knock
over a few useless trees?

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:56.140
We'll beat that thing
to a pulp!

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:58.980
Calm down, you guys!

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:06.740
Captain, even if the
target does head this way...

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:09.240
are you sure it's going
to come out right here?

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:11.580
There's a good chance.
Don't you agree, Yamazaki?

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:18.210
Well, an animal will usually
follow the easiest path.

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:25.130
And all the trails
come out here.

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:28.590
I just hope something
happens before it gets dark.

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:51.910
Which way should I go?

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:55.370
We'll be here forever if
we keep following you.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:57.290
Let's check the
sonograph data.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:00.580
Hey, watch it!

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:04.210
This guy's a real troublemaker!

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:07.550
No kidding!

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:36.080
There's something!

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:37.830
There!

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:49.880
Wait, it's too big, and its heat
signature is too concentrated.

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:53.800
No time for fancy details!
We can't let it escape!

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:56.350
Hold on! It isn't
a living creature.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:58.680
It looks like a
standard-model Labor.

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:01.100
A target's a target.

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:04.190
I'll bet it surrenders
after one shot!

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:09.530
Ota, to your left!

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:10.740
The left!

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:24.750
Bullets!

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:26.880
You don't have
any reserve bullets!

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:29.800
Explain that lousy
marksmanship!

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:32.760
We don't have
any more bullets!

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:34.180
Then I'll use raw strength!

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:38.060
Enough excuses! Your heat
source is getting away!

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:44.440
Those were gunshots.

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:49.070
He fired all six. I'll
bet he didn't hit a thing.

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:53.650
This is command car 2.

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:54.780
Well?

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:56.820
It's on its way.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:00.740
We're handling
the bonus target.

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:01.660
A bonus?

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:02.910
Over and out.

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:06.750
What's she talking about?

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:10.210
Positions, everyone.
Here it comes.

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:11.800
Noa, let's go!

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:17.340
Let's go! We can't
let it get past us!

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:19.300
There they go.

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:21.680
You're sending a
girl on this mission?

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:24.810
That's her job.

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:38.620
Submit!

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:50.420
Let me explain...

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:53.880
We'll handle this!
Go help machine 1!

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:54.800
Roger!

00:17:58.470 --> 00:17:59.510
Target approaching!

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:03.350
200! 150! 100! 50!

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:04.680
Here it comes!

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:05.520
Roger!

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:16.400
Why, you!

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:20.990
What are you doing, Noa?

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:24.080
Come along quietly!

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:25.870
I don't think it understands.

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:43.600
This is horrifying!

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:47.600
Shinshi, Yamazaki.

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:03.950
Spread out...
it's coming back your way.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:06.790
I repeat, it's heading
back toward you.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:10.460
Here it comes!
Grab it!

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:11.830
Roger!

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:22.340
Where'd it go?

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:30.810
Where is it?
Where is it?

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:34.940
Calm down. Animals are most
dangerous when they're cornered.

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:38.650
There it is!

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:54.580
You can't use that
same trick twice!

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:00.510
Noa, use your baton!

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:03.640
You won't get away this time!
Take this!

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:10.100
Good work.
Capture successful.

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:16.060
How dare you kick
my precious Patlabor!

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:25.820
I want a piece of the action!

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:29.080
Take this!

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:34.920
No, Ota, don't!
You'll kill him!

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:37.130
Out of my way!

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:44.430
Don't! That's enough!
He's stopped attacking!

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:47.430
Oh, so you want a
piece of me, too?

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:49.510
That's not what I said!

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:53.100
Then get out of my way!

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:57.230
No, Ota, stop!

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:01.190
Fine, fine. Good work.

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:06.820
Hello?

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:15.830
...so it was a creation of a
medical lab in the mountains.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:19.090
After its growth spurt,
they planned to destroy it...

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:21.710
but the creature escaped, first.

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:25.380
So they tried to
capture it with a Labor?

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:29.350
But when it beat their Labor,
they hauled off the scrap.

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:32.640
They wanted to
hide the evidence.

00:21:32.930 --> 00:21:34.850
What a pain!

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:38.940
They aren't going
to kill him, are they?

00:21:39.310 --> 00:21:43.900
You're worried, after you tried
so hard to beat it to a pulp?

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:47.110
But he hasn't done
anything wrong!

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:50.620
Can they give him to a zoo? Or
maybe a school could raise him.

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:54.080
What was it, anyway?

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:55.710
A bear.

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:57.790
I thought it
looked like a cat.

00:21:58.120 --> 00:22:00.250
I think it was a mole.

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:03.460
No, I think it was a giant rat.

00:22:03.710 --> 00:22:05.260
A grendal.

00:22:05.340 --> 00:22:08.470
No, it was a
giant black panda.

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:09.850
There's no such thing.

00:22:10.100 --> 00:22:12.260
That's because
they just invented it!

00:22:12.430 --> 00:22:14.930
I still think it was a grendal.

00:22:15.390 --> 00:22:17.100
All right, let's go.

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:18.440
Yes, Sir!

